The original [incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) calls this one known parser bug.
The exported reports and tenant directory show two independently fixable causes.
This review covers the 4 October export, not an assurance about the current queue.
Counts below are computed from the source reports, deduplicated by report ID.

<Callout>
Keep parser and booking-form hint failures in separate engineering tickets.
A shared symptom or matching subject is not proof of a shared cause.
Closed does not mean every cause was fixed: see the engineering dispositions below.
</Callout>

## Engineering update: 5 October

The [course challenge page](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows)
now reports **#4471 closed on 5 October**:

| cause | engineering disposition | reason | our ticket closure |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| parser | **FIXED** | `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` | [completed](https://github.com/mmodiG8/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) |
| hint | **WON'T FIX** | booking-v3 form retired | [not planned](https://github.com/mmodiG8/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) |

These are engineering's reported outcomes, not production tests run by this
review. The parser was fixed; the hint was not fixed, because its form was
retired. Preserve that distinction in ticket state, closure comments and this
page. Historical report counts remain the deduplicated export counts.

## What each ticket covers

<CauseTable ticket={4471} {ticketLinks} />

### Parser: tenant day-first dates read month first

The shared parser treats date input as month first even when the tenant locale
is day first. For example, Harbour Dental (`en-GB`, `booking-v2`) reported an
April reminder sent in July in `R-41200`. This is not determined by the
reporter's browser locale or by `meta.intakeTag`.

Reproduce the represented failure by passing an unambiguous intended tenant date,
7 April 2026 entered as `07/04/2026`, through the month-first shared parser:
the result is 4 July, not 7 April. The product runtime is not in this export,
so this is a code-documented reproduction to verify in the product, not a test
we ran against production.

Engineering now reports the parser fix delivered, as shown above. The exported
model's required behavior is tenant-aware parsing or an unambiguous date
representation, covering app/email and `booking-v2` form paths.
A `booking-v3` tenant's app report is still parser, not automatically hint.
Retain the one-day reports below as contrary evidence within this provisional
grouping; the closure notice does not itself reproduce or explain them.

### Hint: booking-v3 instructs month first but reads tenant order

For day-first tenants using `booking-v3`, the form shows `MM/DD/YYYY`, but
interprets what people enter in the tenant's date order. Someone following
that hint for 7 April enters `04/07/2026`; a day-first form reads 4 July.
Only the form channel on that booking version belongs to this cause.

Affected form tenants were Alder Physio, Copper Studio and Pale Harbour.
Engineering retired booking-v3 rather than fixing its hint. If this form is
reintroduced, its hint and input interpretation must agree. Correcting only
the shared parser does not resolve a misleading form instruction.

