## What the desk should do now

Use [decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) and the updated
[triage runbook](/kb/triage/dedupe). Read the body, look up the tenant locale
and booking-form version, then compare the channel and cause. Subject
normalization can find candidate tickets but cannot authorize a merge.
Keep uncertain reports separate for investigation rather than forcing a match.
Keep the two closed tickets and their different resolution reasons as history;
do not describe the retired form as fixed.

When new reports arrive, deduplicate IDs again, recompute both cause counts,
and record the snapshot time. Inspect the received timeline separately from
the merged timeline. Reopen or split the known ticket when a new cause appears;
do not continue accumulating unrelated failures beneath the queued parser fix.
If the one-day investigation establishes another cause, split those IDs and
revise the counts explicitly rather than counting them in two tickets.

